//
// loft#962, the half that pass 2 cannot repair — and it is now an ERROR rather than a
// panic.
//
// Making pass 2 authoritative for a constant's IR (see
// `962-const-initialised-from-a-later-name.loft`) fixes every use that pass 2 reaches
// AFTER the declaration, which is every ordinary program.  It cannot fix a use that pass 2
// reaches BEFORE it: at that point the only value in hand is still pass 1's, and pass 1
// could not resolve `LATER_STILL`.
//
// That case used to paste `Var(u16::MAX)` — the file-scope "no slot" sentinel — and panic
// the variable allocator at `index 65535`, with the caret on an unrelated function.  It is
// refused at the use site instead, naming the constant, its declaration, and the cure.
//
// ⚠ The neighbouring shape must stay legal, and the sibling file pins it: a constant read
// above its declaration is FINE as long as the declaration itself resolves (`fn main() {
// N }` … `const N = 7;` compiles and always has).  Only the compound of the two — read
// above the declaration AND the declaration reaching further down still — is refused.

// @EXPECT_ERROR: constant 'EARLY' is read here, above its declaration

fn main() {
  print("{EARLY}\n");
}

const EARLY: integer = LATER_STILL * 2;
const LATER_STILL: integer = 21;
